cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in a publication, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "dsgelab: a general toolkit for solving DSGE models in Python"
abstract: >-
  Steady state, Klein/QZ first-order solution, second- and third-order perturbation in Dynare's decision-rule form, Chebyshev projection, perfect foresight with expectation errors, optimal policy (Ramsey, discretion, optimal simple rules) and welfare, Kalman filtering and smoothing with mixed-frequency data, Bayesian estimation (Metropolis-Hastings, SMC, HMC and NUTS) and nonlinear filters, local identification, the method of moments, calibration restrictions, global sensitivity, out-of-sample forecast evaluation, shock decompositions and forecasts, plots, reading Dynare .mod files, and export to Dynare and MacroModelling.jl. Validated against Dynare, MacroModelling.jl and closed-form solutions.
authors:
  - family-names: "Moreira"
    given-names: "Gustavo Hoffmann"
    email: "gustavo@gakusai.net"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0827-2521"
version: "0.7.0"
date-released: "2026-10-30"
license: MIT
# The concept DOI on Zenodo resolves to the latest archived release; each release also has a DOI
# of its own (0.5.0: 10.5281/zenodo.23456475). A repository URL is not an archivable reference.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23456474"
repository-code: "https://github.com/GustavoHM/dsgelab"
keywords:
  - "DSGE"
  - "perturbation"
  - "rational expectations"
  - "Python"
